Notebook[
 {Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["HEPCAT SYMBOL", "PacletNameCell"],
       Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["HEPCAT", BaseStyle -> "Link",
           ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/guide/HEPCAT"], "  \[Bullet]  ",
          ButtonBox["Related Guide", BaseStyle -> "Link",
           ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/guide/AmplitudeValidation"]}],
        "AnchorBar"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Right}},
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.42], Scaled[0.58]}}]],
   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["ValidateMadGraph", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Compares exported HEPCAT/SPINAS amplitudes with independent MadGraph \
matrix elements on common random phase-space points, separately for each \
massless-helicity combination.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ValidateMadGraph", "[", "directory",
         "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "builds and runs the MadGraph \
validator of a SPINAS project exported by the current WriteSPINASProcess."}],
   "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ValidateMadGraph", "[", "incoming",
         " ", "->", " ", "outgoing", ",", " ", "entries", ",", " ", "model",
         "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "exports and validates the supplied \
all-incoming amplitude entries for the declared physical process."}],
   "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ValidateMadGraph", "[", "particles",
         ",", " ", "amplitude", ",", " ", "model", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
     "  ", "validates one all-incoming amplitude at its specified massless \
helicities, with IncomingLegs selecting the physical incoming pair."}],
   "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ValidateMadGraph", "[", "input", ",",
         " ", "...", ",", " ", "\"Output\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"Details\"",
         "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "returns the full report, including \
per-helicity failures and the actual random seed."}], "Usage"],
  Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["The default result is a compact \
table with one row for each exported massless-helicity combination. \
\"Output\" -> \"Summary\" gives status counts; \"Output\" -> \"Details\" \
retains the full diagnostic association.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The benchmark is calculated from MadGraph's own generated amplitudes, \
independently of the supplied HEPCAT expression. Both evaluations receive the \
same physical momenta and matched masses and couplings. This tests the \
expression and numerical export together.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Amplitude entries retain HEPCAT's all-incoming convention. Declare \
incoming -> outgoing as in WriteSPINASProcess; the exporter crosses outgoing \
momenta and angle spinors once. Do not cross the formulas manually before \
passing them.", "Notes"], Cell["The particles, amplitude, model overload \
mirrors the original fixed-helicity WriteSPINASProcess form and retains its \
normalization convention. Use the grouped physical-process form when \
validating a complete helicity family.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The reference process is generated without restricting its external \
helicities. The validator selects individual helicity vectors from that \
process, fixes the requested massless helicities and sums the \
massive-particle spin states. It therefore avoids assuming that the MadGraph \
and SPINAS massive spin bases are identical.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The default table displays massless helicities as leg:sign labels, \
such as 3:-, 4:+. A process with no massless helicities is labeled \
accordingly. Details retains the original exported leg-order vectors with \
doubled helicities: photons have entries +2 or -2, and zero entries do not \
select a massless helicity on that leg. Massive spin states are summed.",
   "Notes"], Cell["The comparison uses squared amplitudes. Complex amplitudes \
themselves may differ by external-state phase conventions. Initial spin \
averages and final identical-particle factors are applied consistently once, \
including cases where an incoming or outgoing massless helicity is fixed. \
Multiplying either amplitude by an overall phase, including -1 or I, is not a \
mismatch.", "Notes"], Cell["\"MadGraphPoints\" -> 1000 checks 1000 common \
physical points for each massless-helicity combination. \"MadGraphSeed\" -> \
Automatic chooses a time-based seed at runtime and records it. An explicit \
unsigned 64-bit integer, including zero, permits replay.", "Notes"],
  Cell["\"RelativeTolerance\" -> 10^-7 and \"AbsoluteTolerance\" -> 0 are the \
default comparisons. An absolute floor is not used to hide a wrong small \
amplitude. Nonfinite values, incomplete checks and evaluation errors cannot \
be reported as PASS. A failed report retains the first failing point and its \
momenta.", "Notes"], Cell["\"MinimumEnergy\" and \"MaximumEnergy\" bound the \
sampled center-of-mass energy; Automatic chooses values above the process \
thresholds. These are validation samples, not a phase-space integral or an \
analytic proof.", "Notes"], Cell["Choose \"MadGraphDirectory\" and \
\"MadGraphModel\" explicitly; neither an installation nor a theory is \
selected by default. The model is a UFO name or directory. For example, \
\"sm-full\" includes massive electrons and all Standard Model interactions. \
\"MadGraphAllowedParticles\" -> {11, 22} explicitly restricts that reference \
to the electron, positron and photon sector, excluding Z and Higgs exchange \
in pure-QED four-fermion tests. All, the default filter, retains the complete \
selected theory. Automatic model selection does not infer a theory.",
   "Notes"], Cell["Particle filters use positive absolute PDG codes and \
include the corresponding antiparticles. The list must contain every external \
particle type. A filter that omits an external state or names particles \
unavailable in the selected model cannot produce a passing comparison.",
   "Notes"], Cell["An explicitly supplied Automatic generator directory may \
consult the corresponding environment variables. It does not scan hard-coded \
installation directories. Passing the installation path directly makes the \
reference setup visible in the calculation.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Masses and used model parameters are matched to the supplied model. \
\"MadGraphParameterRules\" -> {\"name\" -> value, ...} overrides named \
external UFO inputs when needed. For a custom theory, ensure that its \
independent inputs and derived couplings agree with the HEPCAT model; \
ambiguous or inconsistent matching produces a diagnostic instead of a false \
pass.", "Notes"], Cell["\"MadGraphParameterMap\" -> {\"HEPCATName\" -> \
\"UFOName\", ...} identifies differently named model parameters. A mapping \
may target an external input or a derived UFO parameter whose value is \
checked. It does not replace the independent numeric inputs supplied by \
MadGraphParameterRules.", "Notes"], Cell["Propagator widths must use the same \
prescription on both sides. Bare HEPCAT PropDen denominators have no decay \
width, so unmatched, independently adjustable MadGraph decay-width inputs are \
set to zero. Explicit MadGraphParameterRules and width parameters used by the \
HEPCAT amplitude retain their supplied values. The detailed Reference report \
records the width policy and the zeroed or preserved inputs; an unsupported \
dependent-width mapping is reported before a comparison can pass.", "Notes"],
  Cell["\"TimeConstraint\" -> 600 bounds MadGraph reference preparation. It \
is not a deadline for the complete export, CMake build and numerical sampling \
operation.", "Notes"], Cell["The current numerical validator supports \
colorless tree-level processes with two incoming particles, at least two \
outgoing particles and external spins through one. It requires MadGraph, a \
Fortran compiler, SPINAS and the normal C++ build tools. Missing \
installations or unsupported inputs are reported explicitly; ordinary \
source-only SPINAS exports remain usable.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Validation can expose numerical conditioning as well as incorrect \
formulas. Expressions involving nearly cancelling terms or inverse small \
masses may lose precision at high energy even when an equivalent compact form \
is stable. Inspect detailed failures before changing tolerances.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The directory overload expects a project containing the MadGraph \
support emitted by the current WriteSPINASProcess. Regenerate an older \
project with that exporter before using this overload.", "Notes"],
  Cell["An exported project retains its process, model parameters, reference \
configuration and fixed-helicity selection. The directory overload changes \
sampling controls such as points, seed, tolerances, energy bounds and the \
reference preparation budget. To change a stored export setting, regenerate \
the project or use the amplitude-and-model overload; those overrides are \
rejected rather than silently ignored.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The same WriteSPINASProcess project can also contain a MadEvent \
numerical launcher. Use ValidateMadGraph for the independent per-helicity \
amplitude comparison and the generated process_madevent launcher for \
numerical integration and event generation with the supplied SPINAS \
amplitude.", "Notes"], Cell["Options", "NotesSection"],
  Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["Option", "TableHeader"],
       Cell["Default", "TableHeader"], Cell["Meaning", "TableHeader"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"SPINASDirectory\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Path to the local SPINAS \
checkout/library. Automatic searches SPINAS_ROOT and the sibling spinas \
checkout; an explicit directory selects another installation.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"IncomingLegs\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "1", ",", " ", "2", "}"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["External leg labels that \
are physically incoming in exported C++. Other legs are crossed once from \
HEPCAT's all-ingoing convention, including outgoing angle-spinor signs. \
Runnable projects currently require two incoming particles.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"FixedHelicities\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Massless \
leg-to-doubled-helicity rules selecting states in the grouped SPINAS \
exporter. Automatic retains the requested coverage; explicitly fixed incoming \
helicities are not averaged over, and a fixed outgoing helicity is a labeled \
contribution.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ParameterRules\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Local numerical parameter \
overrides keyed by model references or string names. Automatic resolves the \
model's variables and dependent functions; fitting and checks do not assign \
global values or replace parameters in the symbolic final amplitude.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProcessName\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"hepcat_process\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Valid C++ identifier for \
the exported SPINAS class and executable. Choose a readable process name that \
does not collide with reserved generated members.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Precision\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Floating-point type used \
by exported SPINAS code. Automatic reads the local library build \
configuration; \"Double\" and \"LongDouble\" must match the library being \
linked.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Build\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether to configure and compile the exported C++ \
project against the existing SPINAS library. False writes source files only; \
a source-only export does not require CMake.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RunExamples\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether to build the exported SPINAS project and \
execute its sample phase-space points. True implies the necessary build \
step.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CMakeExecutable\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Path to the CMake program \
used when building. Automatic searches PATH and standard installations, \
including common macOS application and Homebrew locations.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Overwrite\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether existing generated project files may be \
replaced. False protects an existing SPINAS output directory from accidental \
overwriting.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CalcHEPDirectory\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"None"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Chosen CalcHEP installation directory. None, the \
default, leaves the optional backend unconfigured. An explicitly supplied \
Automatic consults the corresponding environment variables only; no \
installation path is guessed.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CalcHEPModel\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"None"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Chosen equivalent CalcHEP reference theory as \
{directory, modelNumber}. None, the default, selects no theory; Automatic \
does not infer a model. This reference model is separate from the supplied \
HEPCAT amplitudes.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CalcHEPAllowedParticles\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"All"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["All retains the full selected CalcHEP theory. A \
nonempty list of unique positive absolute PDG codes restricts the independent \
reference particle sector, including antiparticles. Every external type must \
be included.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RunCalcHEPValidation\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether export builds and runs the generated \
independent CalcHEP comparison. It uses the same physical points on both \
implementations; unsupported polarized or color-stripped comparisons report \
unavailable. When MadGraph is also requested, its check still runs if CalcHEP \
fails. A failed requested reference returns Failure with both reports \
retained in ExportResult.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CalcHEPPoints\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"1000"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Number of random physical phase-space points \
compared by the generated independent CalcHEP validation executable. This \
tests both implementations at the same points.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CalcHEPSeed\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Default seed of the \
generated CalcHEP comparison. Automatic chooses from the time when validation \
runs and prints the concrete seed; an unsigned 64-bit integer, including \
zero, makes the run reproducible.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ReturnDetails\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether to expose optional diagnostic data \
instead of the compact default result. For preparation and factorization \
completion it retains provenance, directions and validation and takes \
precedence over Output; for export it returns file paths and build/run \
results.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphDirectory\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"None"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Chosen MadGraph installation directory for \
independent validation and the MadEvent numerical bridge. None, the default, \
leaves this optional support unconfigured. An explicitly supplied Automatic \
consults environment variables only; pass a path to make the selection \
explicit.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphModel\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"None"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Chosen MadGraph UFO model name or directory. It \
supplies the independent validation reference and the numerical MadEvent \
model metadata and phase-space topologies. None, the default, selects no \
theory; Automatic does not infer one. Specify the model and any particle \
filter explicitly.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphAllowedParticles\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"All"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["All retains the full selected MadGraph theory. A \
nonempty list of unique positive absolute PDG codes, such as {11,22}, \
restricts the particle sector used for reference validation and MadEvent \
topology generation and includes antiparticles. Every external particle type \
must be present.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphParameterRules\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Real numerical values for \
named external MadGraph UFO parameters. Automatic uses the supported \
model-parameter matching; explicit rules supply otherwise ambiguous \
independent inputs.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphParameterMap\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Rules mapping HEPCAT model \
parameter names to external or derived MadGraph UFO parameter names. \
Automatic uses supported same-name and known-model matching; unresolved used \
parameters prevent a passing comparison.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RunMadGraphValidation\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether WriteSPINASProcess builds and runs the \
independent MadGraph comparison. False writes the optional support without \
running it; True runs a report for each exported massless-helicity \
combination. A numerical FAIL is returned as Failure, not a successful \
source-export result. If CalcHEP is also requested, both checks are attempted \
and their reports remain in ExportResult.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphPoints\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"1000"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Number of common random phase-space points \
compared for each massless-helicity combination. The default is 1000.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphSeed\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Random seed for the \
generated MadGraph comparison. Automatic chooses one time-based seed when \
validation runs and reports it; an explicit unsigned 64-bit integer, \
including zero, replays the samples.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Output\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Table\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Choose the amount and \
shape of returned information. Defaults are a compact check table, prepared \
input forms, a completed {externalMassRules, expression} pair, or a bare \
constructed expression; \"Details\" preserves diagnostics and provenance.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RelativeTolerance\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"1", "/", "10000000"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum relative numerical \
difference allowed by the selected comparison. ValidateMadGraph defaults to \
10^-7; this is applied independently to each tested massless-helicity \
combination.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"AbsoluteTolerance\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"0"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Optional absolute numerical comparison tolerance. \
ValidateMadGraph defaults to zero so a wrong tiny amplitude cannot pass \
through a fixed absolute floor.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MinimumEnergy\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Lower center-of-mass \
energy used by ValidateMadGraph's random validation samples. Automatic \
chooses a value above the incoming and outgoing mass thresholds.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaximumEnergy\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Upper center-of-mass \
energy used by ValidateMadGraph's random validation samples. Automatic \
chooses a suitable range above threshold.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"TimeConstraint\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"600"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Time budget in seconds for generating and \
compiling the independent MadGraph reference process. A timeout is an \
incomplete check, not PASS.", "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment ->
      {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Left}}, GridBoxItemSize ->
      {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.23], Scaled[0.19], Scaled[0.58]}},
     GridBoxDividers -> {"Rows" -> {False, True, {False}, False}}]],
   "3ColumnTableMod"], Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
the local HEPCAT checkout; no model parameters are assigned global numerical \
values.", "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"If", "[", "!", "StringQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", " ", "||", " ", "!", "DirectoryQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ",
         "Global`$HEPCATpath", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "First", "[", "PacletFind", "[", "\"HEPCAT\"", "]", "]", "[",
         "\"Location\"", "]", ",", " ", "\"source\"", "}", "]", "]", ";",
         "\n", "If", "[", "!", "MemberQ", "[", "$Packages", ",", " ",
         "\"ConstructiveDiagrams`\"", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ", "Get", "[",
         "FileNameJoin", "[", "{", "Global`$HEPCATpath", ",", " ",
         "\"HEPCAT.wl\"", "}", "]", "]", "]", ";", "\n", "hepcatDirectory",
         " ", "=", " ", "ParentDirectory", "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]",
         ";", "\n", "modelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[",
         "{", "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"models\"", "}", "]", ";", "\n",
         "feynmanModelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"model_feynman\"", "}", "]", ";"}]],
      "Input", InitializationCell -> True]}, Open]],
  Cell["Basic Examples", "ExampleSection"],
  Cell["Inspect the validation options without running external software.",
   "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Options", "[", "ValidateMadGraph",
      "]"}]], "Input"], Cell["Choose a MadGraph installation and explicitly \
select its QED sector, then validate the complete photon-helicity family. \
Replace this example sibling directory and model selection with your chosen \
installation and theory.", "ExampleText"],
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"madGraphDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin",
      "[", "{", "ParentDirectory", "[", "hepcatDirectory", "]", ",", " ",
      "\"MadGraph\"", "}", "]", ";", "\n", "knownModel", " ", "=", " ",
      "ReadModel", "[", "modelDirectory", ",", " ", "3", "]", ";", "\n",
      "helicityProcesses", " ", "=", " ", "{", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ",
      "\"E\"", ",", " ", "\"A.+\"", ",", " ", "\"A.+\"", "}", ",", " ", "{",
      "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", ",", " ", "\"A.+\"", ",", " ", "\"A.-\"",
      "}", ",", " ", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", ",", " ", "\"A.-\"",
      ",", " ", "\"A.+\"", "}", ",", " ", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"",
      ",", " ", "\"A.-\"", ",", " ", "\"A.-\"", "}", "}", ";", "\n",
      "entries", " ", "=", " ", "{", "#", ",", " ", "LookupAmplitude", "[",
      "Thread", "[", "{", "#", ",", " ", "Range", "[", "4", "]", "}", "]",
      ",", " ", "knownModel", ",", " ", "False", ",", " ", "{", "i1", ",",
      " ", "i2", ",", " ", "i3", ",", " ", "i4", "}", "]", "}", " ", "&",
      " ", "/@", " ", "helicityProcesses", ";", "\n", "ValidateMadGraph",
      "[", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", "}", " ", "->", " ", "{",
      "\"A\"", ",", " ", "\"A\"", "}", ",", " ", "entries", ",", " ",
      "knownModel", ",", " ", "\"MadGraphDirectory\"", " ", "->", " ",
      "madGraphDirectory", ",", " ", "\"MadGraphModel\"", " ", "->", " ",
      "\"sm-full\"", ",", " ", "\"MadGraphAllowedParticles\"", " ", "->",
      " ", "{", "11", ",", " ", "22", "}", "]"}]], "Input"],
  Cell["This example writes files, starts a longer calculation, or requires \
an optional external tool. Evaluate it when you want to perform that \
operation.", "ExampleText"],
  Cell["Replay a run and retain its full diagnostics.", "ExampleText"],
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ValidateMadGraph", "[", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ",
      "\"E\"", "}", " ", "->", " ", "{", "\"A\"", ",", " ", "\"A\"", "}",
      ",", " ", "entries", ",", " ", "knownModel", ",", " ",
      "\"MadGraphDirectory\"", " ", "->", " ", "madGraphDirectory", ",", " ",
      "\"MadGraphModel\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"sm-full\"", ",", " ",
      "\"MadGraphAllowedParticles\"", " ", "->", " ", "{", "11", ",", " ",
      "22", "}", ",", " ", "\"MadGraphSeed\"", " ", "->", " ", "12345", ",",
      " ", "\"Output\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"Details\"", "]"}]], "Input"],
  Cell["This example writes files, starts a longer calculation, or requires \
an optional external tool. Evaluate it when you want to perform that \
operation.", "ExampleText"],
  Cell["Validate a project already written by the current exporter.",
